        "original_id": "9cd78609-1ce1-5f32-be1c-dcc0e22c095f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: P. Susheela, R. Goverdhanam, Ghantasala Venkateswara Rao\n- Works: Ramu (1968 film), \"Raa Raa Krishnayya\"\n- Topics: South Indian cinema, film soundtracks, playback singing\n\nFacts:\n- The 1968 film Ramu had a soundtrack composed by R. Goverdhanam.\n- The songs in Ramu were rendered by Ghantasala Venkateswara Rao and P. Susheela.\n- \"Raa Raa Krishnayya\" is described as the most memorable song from Ramu.\n- P. Susheela is widely acclaimed as a singer who defined feminism in South Indian cinema.\n- P. Susheela is well known for mellifluous vocal performances in more than 40,000 film songs across South Indian languages.",
